1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,020
When you're a person like me, you are fortified.

2
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:10,560
You are somebody who seems to always have it together.

3
00:00:10,780 --> 00:00:13,160
Even when things are falling apart,

4
00:00:13,540 --> 00:00:19,080
you somehow manage to keep things from bursting at the seams.

5
00:00:19,380 --> 00:00:20,940
This ends up working against you

6
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:25,840
because people seem to always think that you don't need them.

7
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:30,120
People seem to always think that you are invincible,

8
00:00:30,520 --> 00:00:32,140
that you are impervious to harm.

9
00:00:32,260 --> 00:00:35,000
And we already know that there is something about this

10
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:37,020
that is applied to Black women in general.

11
00:00:37,180 --> 00:00:38,680
But even in the personal space,

12
00:00:38,840 --> 00:00:42,100
there seems to be this thing where folks really just think,

13
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:44,280
I don't need assistance.

14
00:00:44,740 --> 00:00:50,460
I don't need to be embraced.

15
00:00:50,880 --> 00:00:53,780
And so often, I am embracing myself.

